# Ignore list for THIS Dockerfile only (BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in
# preference to the context root's `.dockerignore`).
#
# Why a second file at all: the repository root `.dockerignore` predates the Node stack and
# does not mention `node_modules`, `.next` or `.npm-cache`. Without them the build context of
# this image carries a few hundred megabytes of host-built dependencies — including
# `@next/swc-darwin-arm64`, a binary that means nothing inside a linux image. The Dockerfile
# never COPYs them, so this is about the size and the honesty of the context, not correctness
# of the result.
#
# KNOWN COST: this file SUPERSEDES the root one for this build, so an entry added at the root
# does not reach here. Mirrored below, and worth re-checking whenever the root file changes.
.git
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
artifacts/
var/
data/
profiles/
codex-home/
*.log
ROADMAP_CODEX_CDP_COMMUNITY_OS.v3-backup.md

# The Node additions the root file does not know about.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.npm-cache
